    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What is a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bubble",
            "ref": "v-bubble"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A soap bubble is a very thin "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "film",
            "zh": "薄膜"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of soap water. Its outside and inside "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "surfaces",
            "ref": "v-surface"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "are made of",
            "ref": "v-made-of"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " soap "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "molecules",
            "zh": "肥皂分子"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". There is a thin "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "layer",
            "zh": "层"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of water between the two layers of soap molecules. It’s like a water sandwich with soap molecules for bread."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Why do bubbles "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pop",
            "zh": "爆裂"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Soap bubbles don’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "last",
            "ref": "v-last"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for very long. They pop when they touch something else. And they pop when the water between the surfaces of the soap film "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "evaporates",
            "zh": "蒸发"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Want your bubbles to last for longer? "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Blow",
            "ref": "v-blow"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " them on a winter day! Water evaporates more slowly when it’s cold."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h3",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Do bubbles have colours?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A bubble looks colourful in the sun. It gets its colours from the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "light waves",
            "zh": "光波"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that are "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "reflected",
            "ref": "v-reflect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " between its two surfaces. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "distance",
            "ref": "v-distance"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " between the surfaces gets smaller "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "as",
            "zh": "随着"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the water evaporates. This makes the colour of the bubble change."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Bubbles can also reflect what’s around them. You can see your face when you look at them!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
